# malscan logical signatures — ClamAV-.ldb-style multi-condition rules.
#
# format:  name ; severity ; techniques ; expression ; sub0 ; sub1 ; ...
#   severity     clean|info|suspicious|malicious  (default: malicious)
#   techniques   comma-separated ATT&CK IDs (may be empty)
#   expression   boolean over subsig indices: & (and), | (or), parentheses
#   subN         str:LITERAL  or  hex (4d5a, ?? = any byte, * = gap)
#
# These are illustrative, low-false-positive rules — the point is to show how
# combining sub-signatures with logic beats any single pattern.

# A PE that imports the classic process-injection trio. Any one import is benign
# (debuggers use them too); all three together is a strong signal.
PE_Injection_Trio ; suspicious ; T1055 ; 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 ; 4d5a ; str:VirtualAllocEx ; str:WriteProcessMemory ; str:CreateRemoteThread

# A PE packed with UPX (either section name present alongside the MZ header).
UPX_Packed_PE ; suspicious ; T1027.002 ; 0 & (1 | 2) ; 4d5a ; str:UPX0 ; str:UPX1

# The EICAR test string expressed as two sub-signatures that must co-occur.
EICAR_Logical ; malicious ; ; 0 & 1 ; str:EICAR-STANDARD-ANTIVIRUS-TEST-FILE ; str:$H+H*
